  "description": "#6530 — `/template` inserts a whole template in one `create_blocks_batch`: a nested spec names its parent by `parentIndex`, the index of an earlier spec in the batch, and a property held as a number, date or boolean rides `typedProperties` into the column of its type. One typed property per spec, as the map is a `HashMap` on the Rust side. The two refusals land nothing: a `parentIndex` that names a later spec is refused before the first write, and an invalid date on the LAST spec refuses the batch after its earlier specs ran, so a stack that is not all-or-nothing leaves the first block in the snapshot.",
